# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.html
coverage.txt
coverage.xml
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# OS and editor clutter: Finder metadata, vim swap files, backup files. `make
# check` reads the working tree and skips what git ignores (C6, R5).
.DS_Store
*.sw[op]
*~

# regcorpus (R5 build output; R1 local download cache; R11 local agent state).
# sources/, registry/ and registry/verify.log stay tracked: in them git ignores
# only what the patterns above ignore anywhere (binaries, test and coverage
# output, go.work, .env, OS and editor clutter) and the temporary files of
# fetch, meta set and parse (below), none of them a corpus file.
/regcorpus
/dist/
# Local raw-download cache: exploratory fetches and the govinfo edition.
# Committed raw XML lives under sources/**/raw/ and stays tracked.
/.cache/
# Temporary files written beside a stored L0 file before it is linked or
# renamed into place (R1; internal/l0/store.go: StoreOnce for `regcorpus
# fetch`, replace, through Update, for `regcorpus meta set` and `regcorpus
# parse`); an interrupted run can leave one behind.
/sources/**/.fetch-*
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
